    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-908" contextRef="c-51">&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 4.6pt; margin-left: 22.75pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 20.55pt; font-weight: bold; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;SUMMARY OF SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: -0.25pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;POLICIES&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.55pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Nature of Operations&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Citizens Sycamore-Penasquitos Transmission, LLC (CSPT or the Company) was formed on June 7, 2017 and is owned 100% by Citizens Enterprises Corporation (Parent). The Company leases 13.1% of the transfer capability of the Underground Segment B portion of the Sycamore-Penasquitos Transmission Line Project from San Diego Gas &amp;amp; Electric (SDG&amp;amp;E). The project includes the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;operation of a 230-kV transmission line between the existing Sycamore Canyon and Penasquitos Substations. The transmission line is maintained by San Diego Gas &amp;amp; Electric (SDG&amp;amp;E), which the Company reimburses for related costs incurred. All of the Company's revenues are from the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) approved Transmission Revenue Requirement (TRR) tariff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;and are collected by the California Independent System Operator (ISO) from users of the transmission line and remitted to the Company.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Accounts Receivable and the Allowance for Credit Losses&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.3pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company leases 13.1% of a transmission line and derives its revenue from a FERC-approved TRR tariff, which is collected by the California ISO from users and is remitted monthly to the Company within 30 days. Accounts receivable are stated at the contractual amount billed to the customer. The Company recognized an allowance for losses on accounts receivable in an amount equal to current expected credit losses. The estimation of the allowance is based on an analysis of historical loss experience, current receivables aging, and management's assessment of current conditions and reasonable and supportable expectation of future conditions, as well as an assessment of specific identifiable customer accounts considered at risk or uncollectible. The Company assesses collectability by pooling receivables where similar characteristics exist and evaluates receivables individually when a specific customer balance no longer shares those risk characteristics and are considered a risk or uncollectible. The expense associated with the allowance for expected credit losses is included in general and administrative&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: -0.05pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;expenses.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.45pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.35pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company has elected an accounting policy to consider subsequent collection activity in measuring expected credit losses. Accordingly, trade receivables that are collected in full after the balance sheet date, but before the date the financial statements are available to be issued are excluded from the credit loss measurement.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.35pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Receivables are written off when information indicates the debtor is experiencing significant financial difficulty and recovery is no longer considered possible. Recoveries of amounts previously written off are recognized in income or as an offset to credit loss expense in the period recovered. Credit losses are expected to be minimal. Accordingly, no provision for credit losses has been included in the financial statements.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.35pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.4pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The preparation of financial statements in conformity with accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect certain reported amounts and disclosures. Accordingly, actual results could differ from those&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.45pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;estimates.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.4pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.55pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.55pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Concentration of Credit Risk&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.5pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Revenues are derived through the TRR which is collected by the California ISO. During the years&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, 100% of the Company's revenue and 100% of the accounts receivable balance at December 31, 2025 and 2024 were derived from the California&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.25pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;ISO.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.4pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Fair Value of Financial Instruments&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.35pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company's financial instruments consist of cash and cash held in escrow, accounts receivable, accounts payable and accrued expenses, and debt instruments. The carrying values of cash and cash &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;held in escrow, accounts receivable, and accounts payable and accrued expenses are generally considered to be representative of their respective fair values because of their short-term nature. The carrying values of the Company's debt instruments approximate their fair values as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, based on the incremental borrowing rates for similar types of borrowing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.2pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;arrangements.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.3pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company recognizes the provision of transmission services in accordance with the TRR as an operating lease with payments depending on the transmission facility being under the operational control of the California ISO. The Company recognizes rental revenue which is shown in the accompanying financial statements as electric revenue while the transmission facility is under the operational control of the California ISO during the term of the lease. The Company's revenue does not fall under the guidance of ASU 2014-09, Revenue from Contracts with Customers (Topic 606) because the standard explicitly excludes lease-based income.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.25pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Deferred Finance Charges&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Interest Topic of the FASB Accounting Standards Codification requires the Company to present deferred finance charges as a reduction of the carrying amount of the debt rather than as an asset (see Note 4). The costs are amortized using the interest method over the life of the debt. Amortization of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;debt issuance costs of approximately $40,000 was charged to interest expense for both of the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024. Amortization of deferred finance charges is expected to be approximately $40,000 per year for the next five&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.05pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;years.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.25pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Prepaid Operating Lease Right-of-Use Asset&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company leases 13.1% of the transfer capability of a transmission line located in San Diego, California. On September 23, 2019, CSPT paid for the 30-year transmission line lease with SDG&amp;amp;E at inception of the lease agreement and is amortizing it on a straight-line basis over the term of the arrangement. The prepaid operating lease right-of-use (ROU) asset is included in current assets and other assets on the Company's balance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: -0.05pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;sheets.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.25pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0.05pt 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;An ROU asset represents the Company's right to use the underlying asset for the lease term. The entire lease obligation was paid-in-full at inception, therefore there is no recognition of a lease liability. Lease expense will be recognized on a straight-line basis over the lease term and the lease does not contain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;any renewal options. The Company does not anticipate that it will need to enter any new leases in the foreseeable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.05pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;future.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.55pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Regulatory Asset&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company is a regulated entity, and in appropriate circumstances, establishes regulatory assets or liabilities, and thereby defers the income statement impact of certain charges or revenues because it is probable to be collected or refunded through future customer billings as required by the Accounting of Certain Types of Regulation Topic of the FASB Accounting Standards Codification. During 2020, the Company received regulatory approval from the FERC to capitalize development and finance costs associated with setting up the transmission project. The Company is amortizing these costs over the thirty-year life of the lease and are reimbursed through the TRR. The over-collections of TRR tariffs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;are returned to rate payers in future rate filings and are classified as a regulatory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.45pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;liability.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.15pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Allocation of Profits, Losses, and Member Distributions&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Profits or losses from operations of the Company, along with gains and losses from the sale, exchange, or other disposition of Company property and tax credits shall be allocated annually to the sole member in accordance with the operating agreement. Net cash flow available for distribution will be paid to the sole member after all conditions contained within the operating agreement have been satisfied.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.4pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Income&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: -0.35pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Taxes&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company is a single-member limited liability company. Therefore, the Company is not liable for federal and state income taxes. All items of income and expense are reflected on the income tax return of its&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: -0.15pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;member.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.45pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Cash Flow Information&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.4pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company considers all highly liquid debt instruments purchased with a maturity of three months or less to be cash equivalents.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.4pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 0.4pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Supplemental disclosure of cash flow information:&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="margin-left: 53.05pt; border-collapse: collapse"&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 11.95pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 273.3pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 101.75pt; border-bottom: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 51.15pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 10.5pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.85pt; border-bottom: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 32.2pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 10.5pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 25.65pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 273.3pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 31.25pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 12.3pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;Cash paid during the years for:&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 52.85pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 12.35pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;Income taxes&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 101.75pt; border-top: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.1pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 5.35pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 12.4pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 58.1pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.85pt; border-top: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.1pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 2.4pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 12.4pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 58.1pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 20.85pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 273.3pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.3pt; margin-left: 52.85pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;Interest&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 101.75pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.3pt; margin-right: 5.35pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 19.45pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;1,126,229&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.85pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.3pt; margin-right: 2.4pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 19.45pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;1,152,120&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 45.2pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 273.3pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 7.5pt; margin-left: 2.5pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Cash and Cash Held in Escrow&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 2.5pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;Cash and cash held in escrow consist of the following:&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 101.75pt; border-bottom: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.45pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-left: 51.15pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 11.05pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.85pt; border-bottom: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.45pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-left: 32.2pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 11.3pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 25.25pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 273.3pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.3pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-left: 52.85pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 11.85pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;Cash&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 101.75pt; border-top: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.2pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 5.35pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 11.85pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 22.2pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;1,500,424&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.85pt; border-top: 0.75pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 32.1pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 1pt"&gt; 							&lt;img src="data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAACAAAAADCAYAAADyQg1sAAAABHNCSVQICAgIfAhkiAAAAAlwSFlzAAAOxAAADsQBlSsOGwAAACpJREFUGJVjZGBgSGSgPzjDwMBwGcb5PwD4FsxyFgYGBn0a+RIfeAZjAAAxSCDYdlWSOAAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==" width="32" height="3" alt="" /&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.1pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-right: 2.4pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 11.85pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 22.2pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;1,378,808&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 12.4pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 273.3pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 52.85pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 11.4pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;Cash held in escrow included in other assets&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 101.75pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 5.35pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 11.4pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 27.7pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;929,670&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.85pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 2.4pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 11.4pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 27.7pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;924,457&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 			&lt;/table&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 120pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Total cash and cash held in escrow shown on the&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 127.15pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 13.1pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="vertical-align: -0.5pt"&gt;statements of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.1pt; vertical-align: -0.5pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: -0.5pt"&gt;cash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.05pt; vertical-align: -0.5pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: -0.5pt"&gt;flows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 115.36pt; vertical-align: -0.5pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 19.5pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; font-size: 10pt; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;2,430,094&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 11.05pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 19.5pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; font-size: 10pt; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;2,303,265&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 4.55pt 11.4pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Amounts included in cash held in escrow represent cash held in a separate account under the terms of a loan agreement with a lender. This lender restriction will lapse when the related long-term debt is paid off.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.55pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Reclassification&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Certain prior year balances have been reclassified to conform with the presentation in the current year.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.55pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Subsequent Events&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.5pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The Company has evaluated subsequent events through April 7, 2026, which is the date the financial statements were available to be issued. No significant matters were identified for disclosure during this evaluation.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.4pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 8pt; margin-left: 40.8pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; text-indent: -18pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Aptos Display&amp;quot;"&gt;2.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 8.83pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Aptos Display&amp;quot;"&gt;PREPAID OPERATING LEASE RIGHT-OF-USE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Aptos Display&amp;quot;; letter-spacing: -0.25pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Aptos Display&amp;quot;"&gt;ASSET&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/h2&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.3pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;On September 23, 2019, CSPT prepaid $27,000,000 for the lease rights to approximately 13% of the transfer capability of the Segment B portion of the Sycamore-Penasquitos 230 Kilovolt Transmission Line from SDG&amp;amp;E, which is a 3 mile underground portion of the transmission line that connects the Sycamore Substation to the Penasquitos Substation, and provides a needed increase of transfer capacity to the Sycamore-Penasquitos service territory.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.25pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0.05pt 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Amortization for both of the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024 amounted to $900,000 and is included in rent expense on the statements of income and member's deficit. Amortization of the prepaid lease for the next five years is expected to be $900,000 per year. Prepaid operating lease ROU asset at December 31, 2025 and 2024 consists of the following:&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.3pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 41.85pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 60.75pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 377.05pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 1pt"&gt; 				&lt;img src="data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAB8AAAADCAYAAABrutTZAAAABHNCSVQICAgIfAhkiAAAAAlwSFlzAAAOxAAADsQBlSsOGwAAADBJREFUGJVjZGBg4GFgYJBnoD+4y8DAwLCJgYHh/wDgNhYGBoZeBgYGFlp7EwtYAgBLyiBe6LifYwAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==" width="31" height="3" alt="" /&gt;&lt;span style="width: 82.8pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAACAAAAADCAYAAADyQg1sAAAABHNCSVQICAgIfAhkiAAAAAlwSFlzAAAOxAAADsQBlSsOGwAAADlJREFUGJVjZIAAVQYGBjYG+oJ3DAwMzxmhnH8MDAyMeBTTAnxhYGDgZYFyVjAwMAjQ2QFHGBgYGAD94QWDYk6ZFAAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==" width="32" height="3" alt="" /&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.5pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="width: 426pt; margin-left: 81.85pt; border-collapse: collapse"&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 12.4pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 256.65pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 2.5pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 11.4pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;Prepaid operating lease ROU asset, current portion&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 89.55pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 5.3pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 11.4pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 30.45pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;900,000&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 2.3pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 11.4pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 30.45pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;900,000&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 12.6pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 256.65pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 2.5pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 11.6pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;Prepaid operating lease ROU asset, noncurrent portion&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 89.55pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 5.3pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 11.6pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 13.9pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;20,475,000&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 2.3pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 11.6pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 13.9pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;21,375,000&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 12.4pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 256.65pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 89.55pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 5.3pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 11.4pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 13.9pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;21,375,000&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 2.3pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 11.4pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 13.9pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;22,275,000&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 			&lt;/table&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 4.6pt; margin-left: 40.8pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;3.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 9.75pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;REGULATORY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: -0.1pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;ASSET&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.55pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 0 11.45pt 0 51.55pt; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;On August 30, 2018, the FERC conditionally accepted in Docket No. ER18-1442-000 the Company's tariff and revenue requirement which included the capitalization of development costs related to CSPT. The FERC approval was subject to a compliance filing to provide the actual cost data. The FERC Order allows amortization of development costs into rates over the thirty-year life of the lease. On March 16, 2020, the FERC accepted in Docket No. ER18-1442-000 the CSPT compliance filing which included capitalization of $1,156,000 of development costs related to CSPT. The compliance filing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;was&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;accepted effective September 23, 2019, the date CSPT obtained its interest in the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.3pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;project.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.15pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Amortization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.55pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;during&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.6pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;both&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.6pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.55pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.6pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;years&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.6pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;ended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.45pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;December&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.4pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;31,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.45pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.45pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.4pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.45pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;amounted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.4pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.5pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;approximately&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;$39,000.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.2pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Amortization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.25pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.25pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.15pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;regulatory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.05pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;asset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.15pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;for&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.15pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.15pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.1pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;five&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.1pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;years&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.1pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;is&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.1pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;expected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.1pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.15pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;be&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 1.15pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;approximately&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 51.55pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;$39,000 per year. Regulatory asset at December 31, 2025 and 2024 consists of the following:&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.5pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 41.85pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right"&gt; 				&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 60.75pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.5pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 4.6pt; margin-right: 18.8pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Regulatory asset,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.15pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.1pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;portion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 122.17pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36.05pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;38,523&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 11pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 36.05pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: -0.05pt"&gt;38,523&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 18.8pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Regulatory asset,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.2pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;noncurrent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="letter-spacing: 0.1pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;portion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 111.22pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 27.7pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; font-size: 10pt; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;876,401&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 16.6pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 27.7pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; font-size: 10pt; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;914,924&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 18.8pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 12.6pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 27.7pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; font-size: 10pt; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;914,924&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 11.05pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 27.75pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Lucida Console&amp;quot;; font-size: 10pt; text-decoration: underline; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;953,447&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.3pt; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="margin-left: 20.65pt; border-collapse: collapse"&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 19.6pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 326.6pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 2.5pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 12.2pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 20.5pt; font-weight: bold; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;LONG-TERM&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: -0.1pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;DEBT&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td colspan="2" rowspan="2" style="width: 160.6pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 19.8pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 326.6pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 6.95pt; margin-left: 31.25pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 11.85pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;Long-term debt consisted of the following at December 31:&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 12.55pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 326.6pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 80.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin: 0 1.8pt 0 3.6pt; text-align: center; line-height: 11.6pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 6.8pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center; line-height: 11.6pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 12.55pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 326.6pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 3.6pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 11.6pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;On September 23, 2019, CSPT issued $30,489,000 of Senior&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 80.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 12.6pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 326.6pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 3.6pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 11.6pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;Secured Notes. These notes call for semi-annual payments of&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 80.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 12.6pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 326.6pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 3.6pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 11.6pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;approximately $890,000, including interest of 4.10% until&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 80.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 12.6pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 326.6pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 3.45pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 11.6pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;October 2049. The notes are secured by a first priority security&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 80.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 12.55pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 326.6pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 3.35pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 11.6pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;interest in all of the Company's assets and are not cross-&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 80.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 12.55pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 326.6pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 3.6pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: right; line-height: 11.6pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;collateralized or guaranteed by any affiliate of the Company.&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 80.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 79.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 12.4pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 326.6pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 31.25pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 11.4pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;(Effective interest rate is 4.45%).&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 80.8pt; vertical-align: top"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 1.8pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center; line-height: 11.4pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 16.65pt; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/